From 35d225843e0aff623c70c22dfa32f17ad2195fcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:06:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 132/270] tegra_audio: playback driver for the Tegra 2 with an
 ALC5632 codec (AC100)

A multi_audio driver for the audio of the Toshiba AC100: PLL A gives the
codec's master clock on CDEV1 and the clock of I2S1, the bus master; the
DAS connects I2S1 to DAP1; an APB DMA channel feeds the I2S1 FIFO in
continuous mode, one buffer after the other; the Realtek ALC5632 on the
first I2C bus is set up as Linux does for the PAZ00, its DAC routed to the
speaker (class D amplifier) and the headphones. 16 bit stereo at 44.1 kHz,
playback only.

tegra_i2c registers the devices the device tree puts on its bus, so that the
driver finds the codec.

For bring-up it logs the clock, pin, DAS and codec setup and plays a short
tone at start.
